'''Raymond C. White''' (May 18, 1949 – April 13, 2025) was an American professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[linebacker]] and [[tight end]] for four seasons in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) for the [[San Diego Chargers]] and [[St. Louis Cardinals (NFL)|St. Louis Cardinals]]. He played [[college football]] for the [[Syracuse Orange football|Syracuse Orange]].
